    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0497" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">585.61B1/574½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-26">June 26, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Lord Halifax<anchor n="28" xml:id="d490-f1"/> called to see me this morning.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador left with me an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi><anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d490-f2"/> expressing the view of the British Government that
                    the International Load-Line Convention should be modified so as to permit
                    cargo-carrying ships, including tankers, to load more deeply than is now
                    permitted under the terms of the Convention. I told the Ambassador that that
                    likewise represented the views of this Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d490-f1" n="28" xml:id="d490-f1-content">
                <p>British Ambassador.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d490-f2" n="29" xml:id="d490-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
